  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Monday)\nIssued at 1241 PM CST TUE NOV 3 2026\n\nBy later this afternoon, our next system approaches as a low \nmoves out of Eastern Kansas across to Iowa and Michigan by \nThursday. As it does so, it will drag a front across much of the \nGulf Coast States including Central Alabama. We could see \nscattered thunderstorms with enough forcing from the front, along \nwith heavy rain at times. Latest guidance looks to weaken storms \nas they get closer tonight with some of the flow potentially slow \nat times with the lower stream system. This is pointing more \ntoward heavy rain/localized flooding potential for tonight into \nWednesday morning than severe, more so in the NW half of Central \nAlabama.\n\nBehind it for Thursday, there will be a small chance for some\nwrap-around showers behind the front as the upper trough pushes\nacross Eastern Conus. Then on Friday a second front, with a small\nto medium chance for a few showers with it, is expected to bring\ndown a much colder Canadian air mass to lower the temperatures\nback into the 40s (and maybe some mid to upper 30s) for lows for\nCentral Alabama as the weekend progresses and into the first part\nof next week. There is a medium chance that we could see our\nfirst frost by Monday night.\n\n16",
